to Syria, Syria to Turkey,

00:02:07.764 --> 00:02:10.884
Turkey to the US, what was
the biggest difference?

00:02:10.884 --> 00:02:12.324
- Turkey.

00:02:12.324 --> 00:02:13.894
- From Syria to Turkey.

00:02:13.894 --> 00:02:14.963
- From Syria to Turkey, because--

00:02:14.963 --> 00:02:15.796
- Why?

00:02:15.796 --> 00:02:17.804
Even more than Turkey to the US?

00:02:17.804 --> 00:02:18.637
- Yes.

00:02:18.637 --> 00:02:19.470
- Go ahead.

00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:22.504
- Because Turkey was very shocking to me,

00:02:22.504 --> 00:02:23.984
it's a new language.

00:02:23.984 --> 00:02:27.414
It's not English, I had to
learn a new language from zero,

00:02:27.414 --> 00:02:29.314
to communicate with people.

00:02:29.314 --> 00:02:30.624
And I was very young,

00:02:30.624 --> 00:02:34.284
I went to Turkey when I
was like 14, fifteen-ish.

00:02:34.284 --> 00:02:38.624
It was my first job there, it
was very tough as a refugee.

00:02:38.624 --> 00:02:41.224
It's literally, you're by your own,

00:02:41.224 --> 00:02:42.364
by yourself, you know.

00:02:42.364 --> 00:02:45.754
And I found myself very responsible,

00:02:45.754 --> 00:02:48.844
I mean in Syria, I was a very
responsible girl growing up,

00:02:48.844 --> 00:02:50.844
because I grew up with a single mom.

00:02:50.844 --> 00:02:53.184
But in Turkey it's like
my mom couldn't hug me,

00:02:53.184 --> 00:02:54.804
because she doesn't know how to hug me.

00:02:54.804 --> 00:02:56.364
So it's like I have to help everyone,

00:02:56.364 --> 00:02:58.011
and that's why it was the hardest.

00:02:58.011 --> 00:02:59.214
- [Gary] It's cool.

00:02:59.214 --> 00:03:01.574
- America, though, I was
kind of ready for it,

00:03:01.574 --> 00:03:03.594
'cause I already learned a lot in Turkey.

00:03:03.594 --> 00:03:05.235
So that's why Turkey was hardest.

00:03:05.235 --> 00:03:07.044
- Makes sense, really cool.

00:03:07.044 --> 00:03:09.387
So you get here and you go where?

00:03:10.394 --> 00:03:14.054
- First I went to
Seattle, but not Seattle,

00:03:14.054 --> 00:03:15.714
like it's a small city around Seattle.

00:03:15.714 --> 00:03:16.764
- Washington State.

00:03:16.764 --> 00:03:18.694
- Washington State, yeah.

00:03:18.694 --> 00:03:19.944
Usually when you're a refugee

00:03:19.944 --> 00:03:21.858
they put you in like a small city.

00:03:21.858 --> 00:03:23.584
- [Gary] Yeah, to get acclimated.

00:03:23.584 --> 00:03:26.784
- Yeah, but it wasn't easy, it was tough.

00:03:26.784 --> 00:03:29.044
So we moved to Michigan,
because it has more Arabs,

00:03:29.044 --> 00:03:31.214
and my mom at least can communicate.

00:03:31.214 --> 00:03:32.124
- [Gary] Yeah, of course.

00:03:32.124 --> 00:03:34.544
- So I studied in Michigan High School.

00:03:34.544 --> 00:03:35.377
- [Gary] Awesome.

00:03:35.377 --> 00:03:37.004
- And my English was very basic,

00:03:37.004 --> 00:03:38.257
and I love to talk, Gary.

00:03:39.154 --> 00:03:40.364
That's why I'm a YouTuber.

00:03:40.364 --> 00:03:41.454
I feel like that's what helped me

00:03:41.454 --> 00:03:43.274
become such a good YouTuber, because--

00:03:43.274 --> 00:03:45.364
- I fear losing my voice more than dying.

00:03:45.364 --> 00:03:46.868
- [Noor] Yeah, right.

00:03:46.868 --> 00:03:49.214
- Like if I couldn't talk,
that would just be like--

00:03:49.214 --> 00:03:51.034
- That's it, we're done (laughs).

00:03:51.034 --> 00:03:52.804
- I mean I'd probably do
some Stephen Hawking shit

00:03:52.804 --> 00:03:55.944
and figure it out, but like,
it would crush my soul.

00:03:55.944 --> 00:03:57.324
- [Noor] Yes, I love to talk.

00:03:57.324 --> 00:03:59.324
- I mean high school's
already tough to begin with

00:03:59.324 --> 00:04:01.341
for people that grow up here,

00:04:01.341 --> 00:04:04.984
like how was your Michigan
high school experience?

00:04:04.984 --> 00:04:07.384
- Oh my God, yeah, as you
said, it's tough by itself.

00:04:07.384 --> 00:04:09.744
So imagine being in high
school without the language.

00:04:09.744 --> 00:04:12.304
And people talk and I'm
like what are you saying?

00:04:12.304 --> 00:04:14.604
I don't understand, like uh, what is this?

00:04:14.604 --> 00:04:17.194
And I went to high school
with the the mindset

00:04:17.194 --> 00:04:20.144
of a Middle-Eastern Arab girl,

00:04:20.144 --> 00:04:22.444
so I was like, what is he saying?

00:04:22.444 --> 00:04:23.714
Flirting, what's flirting?

00:04:23.714 --> 00:04:25.144
I don't get it, like no.

00:04:25.144 --> 00:04:29.194
So I was kind of aggressive
and with no language.

00:04:29.194 --> 00:04:31.644
It was a hard time and I
remember I went to my teacher

00:04:31.644 --> 00:04:34.954
and I was like, look man, I need to speak.

00:04:34.954 --> 00:04:37.124
He keep teaching me like grammar,

00:04:37.124 --> 00:04:40.064
what can I do with the grammar,
grammar doesn't help me.

00:04:40.064 --> 00:04:41.768
- Fuck sentences, I need
to be talking to people.

00:04:41.768 --> 00:04:43.494
- Yeah, I wanna talk,
right, I want to speak.

00:04:43.494 --> 00:04:46.214
And I'm like I need to
speak, I wanna talk to you.

00:04:46.214 --> 00:04:48.184
And he goes like you
have to do extra work.

00:04:48.184 --> 00:04:50.464
I'm like, I'm ready,
give me the extra work.

00:04:50.464 --> 00:04:51.954
- Like I fuckin' worked in Turkey, bro.

00:04:51.954 --> 00:04:53.334
- Yeah, like I wanna learn the language,

00:04:53.334 --> 00:04:55.724
and he goes like here,
there's these websites,

00:04:55.724 --> 00:04:57.324
and listen to music and lyrics,

00:04:57.324 --> 00:04:59.754
and movies and all of
that and then YouTube,

00:04:59.754 --> 00:05:01.504
and he'll give me something on YouTube,

00:05:01.504 --> 00:05:04.564
and that's when I started
binge watching YouTube.

00:05:04.564 --> 00:05:06.794
And I kinda like watched YouTube before,

00:05:06.794 --> 00:05:08.884
but not focused watching YouTube.

00:05:08.884 --> 00:05:11.484
And when I moved to America
I had a lot of free time,

00:05:11.484 --> 00:05:13.104
so I used it, I watched a lot.

00:05:13.104 --> 00:05:16.614
And I remember the first
YouTuber and YouTube video

00:05:16.614 --> 00:05:19.492
that I watched for a
YouTuber that made me like--

00:05:19.492 --> 00:05:20.894
- [Gary] What is this!
- Wait, what is this!

00:05:20.894 --> 00:05:24.074
Exactly, it was from Michelle
Phan, you know Michelle Phan?

00:05:24.074 --> 00:05:24.907
- [Gary] Yes, of course.

00:05:24.907 --> 00:05:28.064
- She's one of the, I met
her last year at VidCon.

00:05:28.064 --> 00:05:28.897
- [Gary] You were pumped?

00:05:28.897 --> 00:05:31.124
- I waited for her and she
came and she's like hi,

00:05:31.124 --> 00:05:33.274
and I was with the Middle East team

00:05:33.274 --> 00:05:35.574
from like Facebook and Instagram,

00:05:35.574 --> 00:05:37.414
and I'm like, guys, leave,
I'm here for something,

00:05:37.414 --> 00:05:38.514
and they were like what's up,

00:05:38.514 --> 00:05:40.114
and I met her.
- That's awesome.

00:05:40.114 --> 00:05:41.414
And I'm like you don't understand,

00:05:41.414 --> 00:05:43.264
your video, the Spanish makeup

00:05:43.264 --> 00:05:45.134
I still remember the video.

00:05:45.134 --> 00:05:47.424
That was the moment when I
was like, that's so cool,

00:05:47.424 --> 00:05:48.434
and I wanna do that.

00:05:48.434 --> 00:05:50.264
I always wanted to do like,

00:05:50.264 --> 00:05:52.874
I always wanted to be in
the entertainment industry.

00:05:52.874 --> 00:05:55.124
But everyone told me it's impossible,

00:05:55.124 --> 00:05:59.364
'cause I'm an Arab girl, first of all--

00:05:59.364 --> 00:06:02.224
- Yes, I'm aware of the
political climate in America.

00:06:02.224 --> 00:06:03.964
- So this is first of all,

00:06:03.964 --> 00:06:04.797
not only in America,

00:06:04.797 --> 00:06:06.644
it's just the culture, you know,

00:06:06.644 --> 00:06:07.914
it's hard for a girl,

00:06:07.914 --> 00:06:09.317
like when I started YouTube,

00:06:10.194 --> 00:06:13.784
girls were only showing
their hands on the internet.

00:06:13.784 --> 00:06:16.614
Rarely you see a girl with her face.

00:06:16.614 --> 00:06:17.704
- [Gary] You mean--

00:06:17.704 --> 00:06:19.384
- In my culture, yeah.

00:06:19.384 --> 00:06:20.864
It's hard, like now it's better now,

00:06:20.864 --> 00:06:24.224
I see girls on YouTube, on
social media, and I'm like wow,

00:06:24.224 --> 00:06:28.214
it's really, we kind of
helped changing this mindset

00:06:28.214 --> 00:06:32.874
and we're still like trying
to, but like from all aspects.

00:06:32.874 --> 00:06:35.977
It's like, Noor, impossible,
go study medical,

00:06:37.093 --> 00:06:38.174
become a doctor, you go to school,

00:06:38.174 --> 00:06:39.814
and I was really good at school,

00:06:39.814 --> 00:06:42.587
straight A student, typical Arab family,

00:06:43.634 --> 00:06:44.974
but honestly I did it for my mom,

00:06:44.974 --> 00:06:45.807
'cause I wanted her to be proud.

00:06:45.807 --> 00:06:46.754
- [Gary] Of course, of course.

00:06:46.754 --> 00:06:48.344
- So I always like get As,

00:06:48.344 --> 00:06:50.714
and yeah, become a doctor, that's it.

00:06:50.714 --> 00:06:52.684
But that's not what I
loved, I didn't wanna.

00:06:52.684 --> 00:06:53.934
- So what happened next?

00:06:53.934 --> 00:06:55.844
You saw the Michelle Phan video,

00:06:55.844 --> 00:06:57.954
how quickly before you
made your first video.

00:06:57.954 --> 00:06:59.234
- Very quick.

00:06:59.234 --> 00:07:00.074
- [Gary] The next day?

00:07:00.074 --> 00:07:02.354
- Yeah, literally, I made a video

00:07:02.354 --> 00:07:05.424
and I remember looking at it
and being like, oh my God,

00:07:05.424 --> 00:07:08.314
I'm gonna put my face on the internet?

00:07:08.314 --> 00:07:09.147
You know what I mean,

00:07:09.147 --> 00:07:11.464
I used to put my face
on Facebook on private,

00:07:11.464 --> 00:07:12.913
only specific people see.

00:07:12.913 --> 00:07:14.974
- Of course, of course, it's cultural.

00:07:14.974 --> 00:07:16.774
But you also were recognizing

00:07:16.774 --> 00:07:19.284
that you were in a new
environment in the US

00:07:19.284 --> 00:07:20.374
that did change,

00:07:20.374 --> 00:07:21.941
like it would have been
far harder to do that.

00:07:21.941 --> 00:07:24.134
- And I was so lonely, Gary,

00:07:24.134 --> 00:07:26.054
honestly, it was a lonely time for me.

00:07:26.054 --> 00:07:28.974
- Look, listen, I know
you know my content,

00:07:28.974 --> 00:07:31.584
a lot of the stuff I say, you know,

00:07:31.584 --> 00:07:34.937
is counter to what parents
and grownups are assuming.

00:07:35.784 --> 00:07:37.884
They don't understand all the benefits

00:07:37.884 --> 00:07:40.084
and virtues of the digital landscape.

00:07:40.084 --> 00:07:41.677
They focus on negatives.

00:07:42.714 --> 00:07:46.034
They're like, kids don't
know how to talk each other

00:07:46.034 --> 00:07:47.324
without using technology.

00:07:47.324 --> 00:07:50.314
I'm like yes, but what
about you sitting lonely

00:07:50.314 --> 00:07:52.614
in Michigan in 1987?

00:07:52.614 --> 00:07:54.084
You'd have stayed fucking lonely.

00:07:54.084 --> 00:07:57.894
- Yeah, I was so lonely
and like very alone.

00:07:57.894 --> 00:08:01.718
It was like, no English, and
that's why I started in Arabic.

00:08:01.718 --> 00:08:02.551
- Interesting.

00:08:02.551 --> 00:08:04.754
- Yeah, I started in my
language that I can do.

00:08:04.754 --> 00:08:05.964
And even though it was tough,

00:08:05.964 --> 00:08:09.434
like I was one of the
first girls on YouTube

00:08:09.434 --> 00:08:10.924
showing their faces.

00:08:10.924 --> 00:08:13.899
And I remember thinking, oh
my God, I'm gonna put this on.

00:08:13.899 --> 00:08:16.404
At the same time I was saying to myself

00:08:16.404 --> 00:08:18.454
I can always make it private.

00:08:18.454 --> 00:08:19.287
- [Gary] Yeah, of course.

00:08:19.287 --> 00:08:22.025
- So it's not gonna go
viral, who's gonna watch it,

00:08:22.025 --> 00:08:23.794
you know, when you tell
yourself, who's gonna watch it?

00:08:23.794 --> 00:08:27.664
And then I uploaded it
and I went and I came back

00:08:27.664 --> 00:08:30.434
and I saw views and people commenting.

00:08:30.434 --> 00:08:32.554
I got, of course, I got hate from people

00:08:32.554 --> 00:08:35.134
saying why is this girl here?

00:08:35.134 --> 00:08:37.704
But also I got a lot
of girls supporting me,

00:08:37.704 --> 00:08:39.314
and that was shocking for me.

00:08:39.314 --> 00:08:41.484
It's like girls, Noor,
we love you, don't stop,

00:08:41.484 --> 00:08:44.404
we want you, we want you
to create more videos.

00:08:44.404 --> 00:08:46.754
And I made my second video
and I made my third video

00:08:46.754 --> 00:08:50.060
and there was no money, I
didn't know the money part.

00:08:50.060 --> 00:08:51.181
- [Gary] Of course, that wasn't the point.

00:08:51.181 --> 00:08:52.734
- No, I was in high school.

00:08:52.734 --> 00:08:54.844
- How often did you post at that point?

00:08:54.844 --> 00:08:57.784
- Not much, when I first started--

00:08:57.784 --> 00:08:59.834
- Like once a month?

00:08:59.834 --> 00:09:02.284
- I don't remember, but
like, not once a month,

00:09:02.284 --> 00:09:05.584
'cause I enjoyed it, I loved
this, so maybe more than that.

00:09:05.584 --> 00:09:09.224
And I got to a point where
I was the first YouTuber

00:09:09.224 --> 00:09:10.074
at least in the Middle East

00:09:10.074 --> 00:09:13.104
that was posting three times a week.

00:09:13.104 --> 00:09:15.033
And other YouTubers,

00:09:15.033 --> 00:09:17.014
like that was doing YouTube at the time,

00:09:17.014 --> 00:09:18.894
they were like why is
this girl posting three,

00:09:18.894 --> 00:09:21.814
'cause usually they post once
a week, once every two weeks,

00:09:21.814 --> 00:09:24.034
and I'm like I love it, I'm
going to post more and more.

00:09:24.034 --> 00:09:26.254
And that's when I passed everyone,

00:09:26.254 --> 00:09:29.244
I start passing people
that has big numbers

00:09:29.244 --> 00:09:30.774
or like have been on YouTube for years

00:09:30.774 --> 00:09:33.964
and I'm like boom, boom, and they text me.

00:09:33.964 --> 00:09:35.144
I remember like one YouTuber,

00:09:35.144 --> 00:09:37.774
he was like bigger than me,
and I tried to talk to him,

00:09:37.774 --> 00:09:39.334
and he's like he didn't talk to me.

00:09:39.334 --> 00:09:40.894
